          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/17/gds-nhs-open-source/\" target=\"_blank\">GDS weighs in on NHS open source decision</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">TechCrunch</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/19/anthropic-acquires-stainless/\" target=\"_blank\">Anthropic acquires Stainless</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        UK Government Digital Service recommends keeping open by default. Making everything private adds delivery costs and reduces reuse and scrutiny.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Anthropic has acquired Stainless, a developer tools startup whose SDKs are used by OpenAI, Google, and Cloudflare. Strategic acquisition gives Anthropic control over critical developer infrastructure.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>open-source</span>",
          "-                        <span>security</span>",
          "-                        <span>gov-uk</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"author\">Kirsten Korosec</div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">anthropic</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">developer-tools</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">acquisitions</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/14/programming-languages-fungible/\" target=\"_blank\">Languages increasingly fungible in agentic era</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">TechCrunch</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/19/elon-musk-loses-lawsuit-sam-altman-openai/\" target=\"_blank\">Musk loses OpenAI lawsuit</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        AI coding agents dramatically reduce migration costs, making technology selection decisions more flexible. Companies can port between platforms more easily.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Court rules in favor of Sam Altman and OpenAI in Elon Musk's lawsuit alleging betrayal of non-profit mission. Validates OpenAI's transition to capped-profit model.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>coding-agents</span>",
          "-                        <span>ai-assisted-programming</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"author\">Tim Fernholz</div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">openai</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">legal</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-governance</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/gitlab-act-2/\" target=\"_blank\">GitLab Act 2: Restructuring for agentic era</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Hacker News</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/composer-2-5\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor Composer 2.5</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        GitLab reorganizes into ~60 smaller teams with end-to-end ownership. 'The agentic era multiplies demand for software' - as production costs collapse, demand will expand.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Cursor releases Composer 2.5 with enhanced AI-assisted programming capabilities. Improvements to code generation, refactoring, and multi-file editing.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>gitlab</span>",
          "-                        <span>coding-agents</span>",
          "-                        <span>organizational-design</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">cursor</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-coding</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">developer-tools</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/ai-coding-maintenance-costs/\" target=\"_blank\">AI coding agents must reduce maintenance costs</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Hacker News</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://archestra.ai/blog/stopping-ai-bot-spam-github\" target=\"_blank\">Stopping AI bot spam in GitHub</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison (quoting James Shore)</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        Critical insight: if you double output and double maintenance costs, you've quadrupled maintenance burden. Math only works if LLM decreases maintenance costs proportionally.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Clever technique for detecting AI-generated bot spam using Git's --author flag to examine commit author metadata for automated submission patterns.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>coding-agents</span>",
          "-                        <span>software-engineering</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">github</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-spam</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/shopify-river-lehrwerkstatt/\" target=\"_blank\">Shopify's River - AI agent in public Slack</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type paper\">ArXiv</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.18609\" target=\"_blank\">AI for Auto-Research</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison (covering Tobias Lütke)</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        Shopify's internal AI coding agent operates only in public Slack channels. 'Lehrwerkstatt' approach - the whole shop floor is the classroom. Learn by osmosis without curriculum.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Comprehensive roadmap for using AI systems to automate research processes. Covers frameworks for leveraging LLMs in literature review, experiment design, and data analysis.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>slack</span>",
          "-                        <span>coding-agents</span>",
          "-                        <span>organizational-learning</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"author\">Lingdong Kong, Xian Sun, Wei Chow, et al.</div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-research</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">automation</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">llms</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/13/ai-agents-meaningless/\" target=\"_blank\">'11 AI agents' is meaningless as a phrase</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type paper\">ArXiv</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.18181\" target=\"_blank\">Scalable Environments Drive Generalizable Agents</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison (quoting Boris Mann)</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        Critiques vague terminology around AI agents. 'I have 11 agents' means about as much as 'I have 11 spreadsheets' - calls for more precise definitions.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        Research on how scalable training environments contribute to developing more generalizable AI agents. Diverse, large-scale environments are key to training adaptive agents.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>ai-agents</span>",
          "-                        <span>terminology</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"author\">Jiayi Zhang, Fanqi Kong, Guibin Zhang, et al.</div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">ai-agents</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">generalization</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">reinforcement-learning</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          " ",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-title\">",
          "-                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/11/zombie-internet/\" target=\"_blank\">Your AI Use Is Breaking My Brain</a>",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"insight-type paper\">ArXiv</span>",
          "+                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.18693\" target=\"_blank\">SkillGenBench</a>",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison (covering Jason Koebler)</div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-description\">",
          "-                        The 'Zombie Internet' concept: people talking to bots, people talking to people, people creating AI agents to interact with people. Filtering AI content is mentally exhausting.",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                        New benchmark for evaluating skill generation in LLM-based agents. Focuses on assessing how well AI agents can acquire and combine new skills to solve complex tasks.",
          "                     </div>",
          "-                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">",
          "-                        <span>ai-ethics</span>",
          "-                        <span>content-quality</span>",
          "+                    <div class=\"author\">Yifan Zhou, Zhentao Zhang, Ziming Cheng, et al.</div>",
          "+                    <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">llm-agents</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">benchmarks</span>",
          "+                        <span class=\"topic\">skill-generation</span>",
          "                     </div>",
          "                 </div>",
          "+",
          "+                <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                    <div class=\"item-title\">",
